2|0@nfl^1439849724#cu6dub0:sighclone$:DC is also just a great place to make the argument strategically, so if they only tossed the name, they'd still likely be a target of groups arguing for it for these reasons: A) The issue is centered around our nation's capital (and thus, it can be implicated, has a higher import/impact on the message it sends). B) The local government of which is unquestionably liberal, and thus, sympathetic to the cause. C) Because it is in DC, it also involves the federal government, so you get national-level politicians commenting on it, raising the profile of the issue. I don't think anything less than completely removing Native American imagery is really going to take heat off the team.
